<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Lalangina</h1><p class="st-meta">1750 CE – 1811 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Betsileo kingdom of the southern Malagasy highlands, one of several small states absorbed by the expanding Merina Kingdom.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Lalangina was one of four main <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/betsileo">Betsileo</a> kingdoms that took shape in the southern highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> in the 18th century, in the region around modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fianarantsoa">Fianarantsoa</a>. Its ruling dynasty claimed descent from immigrant nobles, and its history is known mainly from oral tradition.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/betsileo">Betsileo</a> kings ruled over farming villages that built extensive terraced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> fields in the highland valleys, and royal authority was tied to ancestral tombs and rituals. Lalangina competed with neighbouring kingdoms, including the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-isandra">Kingdom of Isandra</a>, for land and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1811 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/merina-kingdom">Merina Kingdom</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrianampoinimerina">Andrianampoinimerina</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radama-i">Radama I</a> absorbed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/betsileo">Betsileo</a> kingdoms, and Lalangina came under Merina rule. The Betsileo remain one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar's</a> largest peoples.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-lalangina.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Lalangina" width="320" height="232"><figcaption>Image: Randriamamonjy Frédéric · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Betsileo_kingdoms_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1750 CE – 1811 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Malagasy religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malagasy (Betsileo)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/madagascar">Madagascar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lalangina</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1780&amp;focus=kingdom-of-lalangina" aria-label="Kingdom of Lalangina on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5938 2855 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Lalangina lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6286 3134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6258 3111h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6258 3111h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Madagascar. <a href="/atlas?year=1780&amp;focus=kingdom-of-lalangina">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

